-Every upstream socket inherits Android's app_mark for that network and is tagged
+VPN policy: ConnectivityService leaves VPN networks in private-DNS-off mode so
+that their advertised resolver is used inside the tunnel. The saved private DNS
+preference continues to apply to physical networks. Late hostname-bootstrap
+results cannot replace a VPN resolver. A tunnel must advertise a DNS server and
+route to it; a VPN without DNS can still trigger Android's physical-network
+selection. Per-app exclusions and independently implemented DNS remain separate.
+
+Every custom-engine upstream socket inherits Android's app_mark for that network and is tagged
 with AID_DNS. It does not use a global default route or a hostname lookup in Go.
 Android performs the resolver-hostname bootstrap on the corresponding network.
 That initial hostname bootstrap may use that network's DNS. These settings do not
